        <p>
          When the organic feed solution discharges through opposed sapphire micro-orifices (40–80 µm) into pressurized scCO2 at velocities exceeding 100 m/s, the local static pressure drops below the solvent vapor pressure, generating transient micro-bubbles.
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-950 font-mono text-indigo-300 text-[11px] border border-indigo-900/60">
