          In conventional SAS, precipitation is diffusion-limited because the characteristic mixing time tau_mix exceeds nucleation induction time tau_ind (Da &gt; 1.0). In HJC-SAS, extreme turbulent dissipation drives micro-mixing:
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-950 font-mono text-cyan-300 text-[11px] border border-cyan-900/60">
          Da = tau_mix / tau_ind = C * (nu / epsilon)^(1/2) / tau_ind &lt; 0.05
        </div>
